course: dictionary
lesson: 545
title: Attach: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attach means to fix or join one thing to another. You can attach a label to a jar with glue, or a clip, or string. At school you might attach a picture to your page. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Muscles still attach to it, so a fall on it hurts.» Here attach means joined to: the muscles are fixed onto the bone. In «a file attached to an email», attach means added on, as on a computer. The words around it are your clues.
explain: Attach also describes feelings. If you are attached to a pet, you love it and feel fond of it. Some people also attach importance to something, which means they think it matters a lot. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Attach means to fix or join one thing to another.
fact: «Attached» can mean added to something, like a file attached to an email.
fact: To be attached to someone means you love them or feel fond of them.
fact: «Attach importance to» means to think something is very important.
fact: Attach is a verb, and its forms are attach, attaches, attached and attaching.
exercise: «Muscles still attach to it, so a fall on it hurts.» What does attach mean here? | Pull away from | Paint over | Forget about | *Fix or join to
exercise: Sam says, «I have attached my photo to the email.» What did Sam do? | Printed the email | Took the photo off the email | Deleted the email | *Added the photo to the email
exercise: «Ella is very attached to her old teddy bear.» What does attached mean? | Is afraid of | Is tied up with string | *Feels fond of and loves | Is bored with
test: «Quill knobs show where large feathers were attached.» What does attached mean? | *Joined or fixed on | Painted in bright colours | Thrown away | Hidden under the ground
test: Grandad says, «Don't attach so much importance to the score.» What does attach importance mean? | Give the score to a friend | *Think it matters a lot | Write the score down | Forget the score
exam: In «The cat sat on the mat that was black», what is the clause «that was black» attached to? | The room | *The mat | The sofa | The cat
